title: 'omni-node: fix state_traceBlock and state_callRecorded in --dev mode'
doc:
  - audience:
      - Node Dev
      - Node Operator
    description: |
      In `--dev` mode, polkadot-omni-node did not set an executor for block tracing.
      Because of this, `state_traceBlock` failed for blocks with signed extrinsics on
      runtimes that use `StorageWeightReclaim`, and `state_callRecorded` was not available.
      The dev node now uses `ParachainTracingExecuteBlock`, the same executor as the
      normal parachain node.

      Tracing on a dev node now records a proof. This uses more CPU and memory during
      tracing. Block authoring and block import do not change.
crates:
  - name: polkadot-omni-node-lib
    bump: patch
